      {
        "id": 60934,
        "name": "Ronway",
        "username": "Ronway",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/ronway/{size}/1856_2.png",
        "created_at": "2013-05-02T23:14:00.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p><strong>Haka</strong></p><p><strong>HP:</strong> 24</p><p><strong>Hand:&nbsp;</strong> Haka of Shielding, Ground Pound (x2), Savage Mana (x2), Taiaha (x2), Vitality Surge, Haka of Restoration (x2), Haka of Battle, Rampage(x2), Dominion, Elbow Smash, Ta moko (x2)</p><p><strong>In Play</strong>: Taiaha, Dominion (x2), Punish the Weak,</p><p><strong>Trash</strong>: Haka of Shielding (x3), Enduring Intercession(x2), Punish the Weak, Vitality Surge(x2), Haka of Battle, Haka of Restoration (x2), Savage Mana</p><p>-----------------</p><p><strong>Start of Hero Turn</strong>: nothing</p><p><strong>Play a Card:</strong> Rampage!!! Destroys the bonds, which sadly trigger Akash'Bhuta. Which plays Disrupt the Field, which destroys all environment cards (there are no more) And play the top of both villain and environment decks. Earths Sacrifice, we have to destroy 4 ongoings. Dominions, Otherworldly Resilience, and Research Grant will be destroyed. The Environment card played is Time Flies!!! So now heroes can play 2 cards and draw 2 cards on the respective phases. Rampage continues its damage Carapace (5), Phalanges (8), Akash (118). Heroes will all take 1 damage Tempest (20), Haka (23), Tachyon (20), NightMist (20). For the second card Haka will Rampage again!!! Destroying the Carapace, causing Akash to hit herself (107), Phalanges (2), and Akash (103).</p><p><strong>Use a Power:</strong> Taiha the Phalanges destroying it dealing 12 damage to Akash (91), and then Taiahaing Akash for 4 (87).</p><p><strong>Draw a Card:</strong> Dominion and Haka of Restoration.</p><p><strong>End of Hero Turn</strong>: none</p><p>-----------------</p><p><strong>HP:</strong> 24</p><p><strong>Hand:&nbsp;</strong> Haka of Shielding, Ground Pound (x2), Savage Mana (x2), Taiaha (x2), Vitality Surge, Haka of Restoration (x3), Haka of Battle, Rampage, Dominion, Elbow Smash, Ta moko (x2)</p><p><strong>In Play</strong>: Taiaha, Punish the Weak</p><p><strong>Trash</strong>: Haka of Shielding (x3), Enduring Intercession(x2), Punish the Weak, Vitality Surge(x2), Haka of Battle, Haka of Restoration (x2), Savage Mana, Rampage (x2)</p><p>-----------------</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Notes:</strong>&nbsp;Now we can play 2! Woohoo! Pydro I think Mistbounding is a great idea. And if your last turn is correct it says you have two of them. Maybe Mistbounding both the Villain and Environment decks thus it will pretty much go back to Tempest and we may have it won next turn. Tachyon can focus this turn getting the last few burst cards in the trash along with getting the precious last Light-Speed barrage!</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Edit: One more thing NightMist didn't need to redirect as Time Flies allowed Haka to take it out without a sweat, though next turn may be a bit different!</p>",
